Natural Language Processing (NLP)
Definition

Natural Language Processing (NLP) is a branch of Artificial Intelligence (AI) that enables computers to understand, interpret, analyze, and process human languages.

In simple terms, NLP helps computers understand the language humans use for communication.

NLP in Action

Consider the customer message:

"The product quality is very good, but delivery was delayed."

A normal computer sees this as a collection of text characters.

Using NLP, the system can understand the meaning of the sentence and identify:

Product Quality → Positive Opinion ✅
Delivery → Negative Opinion ❌

Thus, NLP helps computers understand human communication and extract meaningful information from text.

Why is NLP Required in UiPath?

Traditional RPA works mainly with:

Structured data
Fixed rules
Predefined instructions

However, businesses receive large amounts of unstructured data, such as:

Customer feedback
Emails
PDF documents
Chat messages
Support requests
Survey responses

NLP helps UiPath workflows understand and process this text data and make intelligent decisions automatically.

NLP + UiPath: Customer Email Processing

Consider an organization receiving hundreds of customer emails daily.

The process works as follows:

Step 1: Read Emails

UiPath reads customer emails automatically.

Step 2: Analyze Text

NLP analyzes the content of the email.

Step 3: Identify Category

The system determines whether the email is:

Complaint
Enquiry
Appreciation
Step 4: Take Action

UiPath automatically forwards the email to the appropriate department.

Therefore, NLP makes RPA workflows more intelligent and capable of handling unstructured text.
